[
  "7:0 metadata-line ...",
  "13:0 metadata-line Markdown is a plain text format for writing structured docum",
  "14:0 metadata-line based on conventions for indicating formatting in email",
  "15:0 metadata-line and usenet posts.  It was developed by John Gruber (with",
  "16:0 metadata-line help from Aaron Swartz) and released in 2004 in the form of ",
  "17:0 metadata-line [syntax description](https://daringfireball.net/projects/mar",
  "18:0 metadata-line and a Perl script (\`Markdown.pl\`) for converting Markdown to",
  "19:0 metadata-line HTML.  In the next decade, dozens of implementations were",
  "20:0 metadata-line developed in many languages.  Some extended the original",
  "21:0 metadata-line Markdown syntax with conventions for footnotes, tables, and",
  "22:0 metadata-line other document elements.  Some allowed Markdown documents to",
  "23:0 metadata-line rendered in formats other than HTML.  Websites like Reddit,",
  "24:0 metadata-line StackOverflow, and GitHub had millions of people using Markd",
  "25:0 metadata-line And Markdown started to be used beyond the web, to author bo",
  "26:0 metadata-line articles, slide shows, letters, and lecture notes.",
  "28:0 metadata-line What distinguishes Markdown from many other lightweight mark",
  "29:0 metadata-line syntaxes, which are often easier to write, is its readabilit",
  "30:0 metadata-line As Gruber writes:",
  "32:0 metadata-line > The overriding design goal for Markdown's formatting synta",
  "33:0 metadata-line > to make it as readable as possible. The idea is that a",
  "34:0 metadata-line > Markdown-formatted document should be publishable as-is, a",
  "35:0 metadata-line > plain text, without looking like it's been marked up with ",
  "36:0 metadata-line > or formatting instructions.",
  "37:0 metadata-line > (<https://daringfireball.net/projects/markdown/>)",
  "39:0 metadata-line The point can be illustrated by comparing a sample of",
  "40:0 metadata-line [AsciiDoc](https://asciidoc.org/) with",
  "41:0 metadata-line an equivalent sample of Markdown.  Here is a sample of",
  "42:0 metadata-line AsciiDoc from the AsciiDoc manual:",
  "44:0 metadata-line \`\`\`",
